  "major": "africana-studies-ba-2214c170",
  "major_name": "Africana Studies",
  "degree": "BA",
  "campus": "Boston",
  "college": "College of Social Sciences and Humanities",
  "overview_text": "Africana studies is an interdisciplinary field of study that is focused on the experience of Black people throughout the world. This includes people and cultures identified as African, African American, Latin American, Black European, and Caribbean. The field is devoted to the critical and systematic examination of the cultural, political, social, economic, and historical experiences of the African diaspora across the globe.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nBA Language Requirements\nAll BA students are required to complete the BA degree language requirements, for a total of 12 semester hours of language study or demonstrated equivalent proficiency, as described in\nAdditional Requirements for BA students\n. Successful demonstration of proficiency does not reduce total minimum semester hours of study required to earn the BA degree.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nMajor Requirements\nPlease contact africanastudies@northeastern.edu if you see a class (with or without the AFCS prefix) that you believe would apply to any of the requirements below but is not listed. We are more than happy to consider exceptions.\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nIntroduction to Africana Studies\nAFCS 1101\nIntroduction to African American and Africana Studies\n4\nApproaches to the Field\nComplete two of the following:\n8\nAFCS 1140\nIntroduction to African-American History\nAFCS 1225\nGender, Race, and Medicine\nAFCS 1270\nIntroduction to Global Health\nAFCS 2270\nRace, Ethnicity, and Inequality\nAFCS 2325\nBlack Feminist Studies\nAFCS 2600\nIssues in Race, Science, and Technology\nAFCS 3120\nRace, Crime, and Justice\nAFCS 3305\nBeyond the Binary: Race, Sex, and Science\nAFCS 3323\nRace, Inequality, and the Law\nAFCS 5001\nSpecial Topics in Race and the Law\nAFCS 5544\nSeminar in Black Leadership\nExploring Intellectual Traditions and Cultural Production\nComplete three of the following:\n12\nAFCS 1113\nBlack Popular Culture\nAFCS 2296\nEarly African-American Literature\nAFCS 2455\nAmerican Women Writers\nAFCS 2619\nRace and Religion in Film\nAFCS 2690\nBoston in Literature\nAFCS 3404\nAfrican American Rhetorical Traditions\nAFCS 3664\nBlack Poetry and the Spoken Word\nAFCS 3900\nGender and Black World Literatures\nAFCS 4588\nLiterature in Context\nUnderstanding Society and Social Movements\nComplete three of the following:\n12\nAFCS 1261\nGlobal Caribbean\nAFCS 2318\nNew England Stories: Storytelling and the African American Experience\nAFCS 2325\nBlack Feminist Studies\nAFCS 2330\nAfro-Latin American Studies\nAFCS 2337\nAfrican American History Before 1900\nAFCS 2355\nRace, Identity, Social Change, and Empowerment\nAFCS 2380\nBlack Families and Incarceration\nAFCS 2390\nAfrica and the World in Early Times\nAFCS 2410\nPossession, Sacrifice, and Divination in African Diasporic Religions\nAFCS 2900\nSwahili, Culture, and Politics in Kenya\nAFCS 3424\nEpidemiology of Pandemic Diseases and Health Disparities in the African Diaspora\nAFCS 4526\nAfro-Asian Relations in the Americas\nAFCS 4939\nCommunity Health, Culture, and Development in Kenya\nElectives\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one AFCS course at the 2000 level or above.\n4\nComplete one AFCS course at the 3000 level or above.\n4\nCapstone Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nAFCS 4700\nCapstone\n4\nAfricana Studies Major Credit Requirements\nComplete 48 semester hours in the major.\nExperiential Liberal Arts\nAll students in this College of Social Sciences and Humanities program are required to complete the\nExperiential Liberal Arts Requirement\n.\nProgram Requirements\n128 total semester hours required",
